## Predict Questions:


helm install team ./serving-chart then helm install shadow ./serving-chart: what exists in the cluster that could not exist with plain kubectl apply of the same YAML twice? 
  > twice 
The HPA targets 50% of a 250m CPU request. Your load pushes each pod to ~300m. How many replicas does the controller want? (The formula is in the deck; do the arithmetic.)
  > Target = 50% of 250m = 125m. Usage = 300m. Ratio = 300/125 = 2.4 → ceil = 3 replicas
When the load stops, do replicas drop immediately? What is the risk if they did?
  > No, replicas don't drop immediately. scaleDownStabilizationSeconds first. Risk if it did drop instantly: flapping a brief dip in load kills a pod, then load ticks back up and it has to spin up again, 
    causing thrashing and repeated cold-starts instead of stable capacity.
